# ATLAS Academy — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values from your Supabase project:
#   Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API
#
# Everything prefixed VITE_ is bundled into the JavaScript sent to the browser.
# Never put a secret behind a VITE_ prefix.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client — safe to expose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The "anon" / "publishable" key. This key is public by design; it identifies
# the project, not the user. Every permission is enforced by Row Level Security
# in the database, so the anon key on its own grants access to nothing.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server only — never expose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The service-role key bypasses Row Level Security completely.
#
# Nothing in this application uses it, and nothing needs it. Accounts are
# created in the Supabase dashboard — see LAUNCH.md step 8. It is named here
# only so the rule is written down somewhere: if a server-side function ever
# does need it, it belongs in that function's own environment, never in this
# file, never under src/, and never behind a VITE_ prefix.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
